#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:41
#, fuzzy
msgid "DMARC, or Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting, and Conformance, is an email authentication protocol that allows domain owners to protect their domain from unauthorized use, such as spam and phishing attacks. It is important because it helps protect against these types of cyber threats and helps ensure the authenticity of emails from a specific domain. This helps prevent email spoofing, which is when attackers send emails that appear to be from a legitimate source but are actually fraudulent. DMARC also provides reporting and feedback mechanisms to help domain owners monitor and improve their email authentication practices."
msgstr "DMARC, au Uthibitishaji wa Ujumbe unaotegemea Kikoa, Kuripoti, na Kufuata, ni itifaki ya uthibitishaji wa barua pepe ambayo inaruhusu wamiliki wa kikoa kulinda kikoa chao kutokana na matumizi yasiyoidhinishwa, kama vile spam na mashambulizi ya uwongo. Ni muhimu kwa sababu inasaidia kulinda dhidi ya aina hizi za vitisho vya mtandao na husaidia kuhakikisha uhalali wa barua pepe kutoka kwa uwanja maalum. Hii inasaidia kuzuia uharibifu wa barua pepe, ambayo ni wakati washambuliaji hutuma barua pepe ambazo zinaonekana kutoka kwa chanzo halali lakini kwa kweli ni udanganyifu. DMARC pia hutoa taratibu za kuripoti na maoni ili kusaidia wamiliki wa kikoa kufuatilia na kuboresha mazoea yao ya uthibitishaji wa barua pepe."

#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:43
#, fuzzy
msgid "A sender policy framework (SPF) is a security protocol that helps prevent email spoofing by verifying the sender's identity and ensuring that the email is being sent from an authorized server. This is important because email spoofing is a common tactic used by cybercriminals to send fraudulent or malicious emails that appear to be from legitimate sources, such as a bank or government agency. SPF helps to protect individuals and organizations from these types of scams, by ensuring that the sender's identity is authentic and the email is coming from a trusted source."
msgstr "Mfumo wa sera ya mtumaji (SPF) ni itifaki ya usalama ambayo husaidia kuzuia uharibifu wa barua pepe kwa kuthibitisha utambulisho wa mtumaji na kuhakikisha kuwa barua pepe inatumwa kutoka kwa seva iliyoidhinishwa. Hii ni muhimu kwa sababu upigaji wa barua pepe ni mbinu ya kawaida inayotumiwa na wahalifu wa mtandao kutuma barua pepe za udanganyifu au zenye nia mbaya ambazo zinaonekana kutoka vyanzo halali, kama vile benki au wakala wa serikali. SPF husaidia kulinda watu binafsi na mashirika dhidi ya aina hizi za utapeli, kwa kuhakikisha kuwa utambulisho wa mtumaji ni halisi na barua pepe inatoka kwa chanzo cha kuaminika."

#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:45
#, fuzzy
msgid "DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail) is an email authentication technique that uses a digital signature to verify that an email message has not been altered during transit. It is important because it helps protect against spam, phishing, and other types of email fraud. By verifying the authenticity of an email message, DKIM helps ensure that the sender is who they claim to be, and that the message has not been tampered with. This helps to prevent malicious actors from sending fake or fraudulent emails that could potentially harm the recipient. Overall, DKIM is an important tool for securing email communications and protecting against cyber threats."
msgstr "DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail) ni mbinu ya uthibitishaji wa barua pepe ambayo hutumia saini ya dijiti kuthibitisha kuwa ujumbe wa barua pepe haujabadilishwa wakati wa usafirishaji. Ni muhimu kwa sababu inasaidia kulinda dhidi ya spam, hadaa, na aina nyingine za udanganyifu wa barua pepe. Kwa kuthibitisha uhalisia wa ujumbe wa barua pepe, DKIM husaidia kuhakikisha kuwa mtumaji ni nani wanadai kuwa, na kwamba ujumbe haujavurugwa. Hii inasaidia kuzuia watendaji wenye nia mbaya kutuma barua pepe bandia au za udanganyifu ambazo zinaweza kumdhuru mpokeaji. Kwa ujumla, DKIM ni chombo muhimu cha kupata mawasiliano ya barua pepe na kulinda dhidi ya vitisho vya mtandao."

#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:47
#, fuzzy
msgid "Domain age refers to the length of time that a domain name has been registered and in use. It is important for the domain reputation because older domains tend to have a better reputation and are generally more trustworthy. This is because older domains have had more time to establish themselves, build up a positive online presence, and develop a good reputation. Additionally, newer domains are often considered less credible and authoritative because they didn’t have the time to build an audience."
msgstr "Umri wa kikoa unahusu urefu wa muda ambao jina la kikoa limesajiliwa na linatumika. Ni muhimu kwa sifa ya kikoa kwa sababu vikoa vya zamani huwa na sifa bora na kwa ujumla ni ya kuaminika zaidi. Hii ni kwa sababu vikoa vya zamani vimekuwa na muda zaidi wa kujiimarisha, kujenga uwepo mzuri mtandaoni, na kuendeleza sifa nzuri. Zaidi ya hayo, vikoa vipya mara nyingi huchukuliwa kuwa chini ya kuaminika na mamlaka kwa sababu hawakuwa na wakati wa kujenga hadhira."

